.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH GOLDENRECORD 1 2000-Jan "decode" "decode"
.SH NAME
decode \- Decode the wav data as the image pixels
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIdecode(\fBwav\fR as <generic> WaveFile,
\fBchunk\fR as <generic> ImageChunk,
\fBdecode\fR as <generic> DecoderArgument,
\fBsize\fR as integer = 0,
\fBoffsetLeft\fR as double = 0.2,
\fBoffsetRight\fR as double = 0.2,
\fBpixels\fR as integer = 0,
\fBlines\fR as integer = 0,
\fBalign\fR as boolean = TRUE,
\fBguard\fR as double = 0,
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Decode the wav data as the image pixels
.PP
the scan line period and the pixel clock are measured from the waveform data
itself (see the \fBdecode.report\fR function for the empirical analysis), the
\fBoffsetLeft\fR/\fBoffsetRight\fR parameters of the original implementation are
kept only for the backward compatibility of the existing scripts.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBwav\fB \fR\- -.
.PP
.PP
\fBchunk\fB \fR\- the image data section on the wave file.
.PP
.PP
\fBdecode\fB \fR\- the decoder arguments, the invalid values are filled by the measured ones.
.PP
.PP
\fBsize\fB \fR\- 0. the pixel cells (the image rows) per scan line, 0 for the default 364.
.PP
.PP
\fBoffsetLeft\fB \fR\- 0.2. the legacy parameter of the original implementation.
.PP
.PP
\fBoffsetRight\fB \fR\- 0.2. the legacy parameter of the original implementation.
.PP
.PP
\fBpixels\fB \fR\- 0. the alias of the \fBsize\fR parameter, the value of \fBsize\fR wins when both are assigned.
.PP
.PP
\fBlines\fB \fR\- 0. the number of the scan lines (the image columns), 0 for the default 512.
.PP
.PP
\fBalign\fB \fR\- TRUE. apply the per scan line synchronization.
.PP
.PP
\fBguard\fB \fR\- 0. the samples which are skipped after the sync pulse position.
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- -.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
goldenRecord
.SH FILES
.PP
voyager-1.dll
.PP
